  {
    "id": "3819203111",
    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "Matrix 3D Rain WebGL",
    "description": "Matrix-style digital rain in 3D, drawn with WebGL. Drops fall at different distances onto a reflective water plane, where they splash and make ripples, and fade into layers of drifting fog that blur what is behind them. Now and then lightning strikes, lighting up the sky and the water. A clock and a message can be shown, formed by the rain that freezes inside their letters.\n\n[h1]Customizable elements:[/h1]\n[h3]Rain[/h3]\n[list]\n    [*]Drops: characters, density, frequency, speed and trail length, falling in columns at different distances\n    [*]Distance: font size range; smaller drops are further back, slower and dimmer\n    [*]Glow: head brightness and bloom, both stronger at the front\n    [*]Colors: 4 custom colors or a rainbow color wave (speed and width), high contrast text\n    [*]Lightning: playing time, brightness, flash intensity and average time between strikes; branching bolts at random places and distances, several at once, as a glowing line or made of rain characters\n[/list]\n[h3]Physics[/h3]\n[list]\n    [*]Planes: height and tone; a collision plane where drops land and a reflection plane that mirrors the rain, the lightning and the text\n    [*]Splashes: height; they fly forwards, backwards and sideways in 3D\n    [*]Reflection: strength, up to mirror-like\n    [*]Ripples: intensity, darkening, lightening, speed and duration of the rings spreading on the water\n    [*]Distance fog: two colors, intensity, blurring, number of layers and movement; drifting layers that cover and blur what is behind them\n[/list]\n[h3]Music[/h3]\n[list]\n    [*]Reaction: sensitivity of the rain and of the lightning; both react to the music that is playing, with strikes on its sudden, loud peaks\n    [*]Idle animation: after a set time of silence, the rain and the lightning go on as without music\n[/list]\n[h3]Clock[/h3]\n[list]\n    [*]Clock: 24h or 12h, formed by the rain that freezes inside its digits, never covered by the fog\n    [*]Size and position: absolute, or relative to the screen\n[/list]\n[h3]Message[/h3]\n[list]\n    [*]Message: custom text, formed by the frozen rain like the clock, shown with the clock or on its own\n    [*]Size and position: absolute, or relative to the screen\n[/list]\n[h3]Miscellaneous[/h3]\n[list]\n    [*]OLED pixel shift: moves the rain and the text a few pixels now and then, against burn-in\n    [*]Frame cap: 24 FPS recommended for the film look\n[/list]",
    "author": {
      "name": "",
      "steamId": "76561198074099890"
    },
